# Domain module topology (target state)

Each module under `src/domains/<module>/` is a vertical slice with this layer shape and a **single public `index.ts` barrel**:

```
src/domains/<module>/
├── ui/           # React components (presentational + container)
├── state/        # Zustand client UI state; TanStack Query for server data
├── io/           # network/api boundaries
├── core/         # pure domain logic (no React, no DB, no IO)
├── services/     # orchestration / business services
├── agents/       # Mastra agents + tools (domain-specific)
├── tasks/        # Trigger.dev tasks (asset modules lean here, not agents/)
├── prompts/      # agent prompts + Workspace skills
└── index.ts      # single public barrel
```

## Dependency rule (inward → outward allowed; outward → inward forbidden)

`ui → state → io → core → services → agents`, and `ui` may read `services`/`agents` only via the barrel. **Never**: `ui` touching `db`/`io` directly, `core` importing React/DB/IO, cross-module internal (non-barrel) imports.

## Non-negotiable invariants

1. One public `index.ts` barrel per module — no deep imports from outside.
2. Server data lives in Tanstack Query, **not** Zustand.
3. Browser → Supabase writes go through the sanctioned write path; no manual snake_case remapping scattered in components.
4. One framework — don't hand-roll parallels to Mastra primitives (agents, memory, tools, workflows).
5. Typed boundaries — no `any` at module edges; no `z.any()` in workflow/agent schemas.
6. File size limits — no god files (split beyond ~300-400 lines).
7. ESLint barrel guards (`no-restricted-imports`) per module — storyteller has one; add for new modules.
8. Asset modules (`interior-designer`, `world-building-toolkit`, `3d-asset-exporter`) lean on `tasks/` not `agents/`.

## When changing a module

- Place every change in the correct layer above.
- Name the barrel contract you touch.
- Flag any step crossing a dependency-rule boundary as a risk in `PLAN.md`.
- Run `node scripts/fabro-verify.mjs` — it scopes to the module and ignores out-of-scope errors.

Governing doc: `docs/unified/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
